            <div id="pnlSpecialRequirements">
	
                <h3 class="postingHeader">Special Requirements</h3>
                <div class="postingContent">
		
                    <ul>
                        
                        
                        <li id="rowSpecialRequirementCDL">
                            <span id="lblSpecialRequirement_ValidCDL">The position(s) require(s) a valid California Drivers License (CDL).  You must answer the questions addressing your CDL on your application.  Ensure you provide your CDL number, class, expiration date, and any endorsements and/or restrictions.</span></li>
                        
                        
                        
                        
                        

                        
                                <li>The position(s) require(s) a(n) California Land Surveyors' License License.  You will be required to provide a copy of your license prior to being hired.</li>
                            
                        
                    </ul>
                
	</div>
                <div class="postingContent">
                    <span id="lblSpecialRequirementText"><p class="MsoListParagraph" style="margin:0in;mso-add-space:auto;line-height:&#xA;normal"><span style="font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"></span></p> <p class="MsoListParagraph" style="margin:0in;mso-add-space:auto;line-height:&#xA;normal"><span style="font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif"> <strong>Possession of a valid California Land Surveyors&#39; License. A Certificate of Registration as a Civil Engineer issued by the California Board of Registration for Professional Engineers and Land Surveyors.<br /><br /> </strong></span></p><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><strong>Statement of Qualifications (SOQ) -</strong> Applicants are required to submit a SOQ. The SOQ is a discussion of how an applicant’s education, training, experience, and skills meet the criteria in the duty statement to qualify the candidate for the position. The one-page SOQ must be typed in size 11 font. <strong>Resumes and cover letters will not take place of the SOQ. Failure to include and complete the SOQ may result in disqualification for interview.</strong></span></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><br /></span></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;">The SOQ will address the candidate&#39;s experience in the following areas:</span></div><span style="font-size: 12pt;"> </span><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;">1. Demonstrated experience as a land surveys lead-worker. Demonstrated ability to work in a team environment including field and office experience.  Working with public and state agencies, contractors, and the public.</span></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;">2. Demonstrated field experience performing H&amp;V control, boundary, Digital Terrain Model (DTM) topographic, monitoring, aerial photogrammetric and construction surveys.</span></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;">3. Demonstrated experience to balance multiple priorities and meet strict deadlines, organize tools and equipment, maintain records, track schedules and manage staff.</span></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;">4. Knowledge of Land Surveying techniques for both field and office, mathematical principles and concepts.</span></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;">5. Demonstrated experience  working with software including Civil3D, Microstation, TopoDOT,  Trimble Businss Center and Trimble Access, Microsoft Office suite, and any Geographic Information Systems (GIS).</span></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;">6. Demonstrated experience working with various field surveying systems including Terrestrial, Global Navigation Satellite Systems (GNSS) and  Unmanned Aircraft Systems (UAS)</span></div><div><span style="font-size: 12pt;">7. Demonstrated Office Experience, including Digital Terrain Model processing, point cloud registration and extraction, Record Map preparation, boundary determination, deed writing, record research, construction plan interpretation<br /><br /> <span style="font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"> </span></span> </div><div><br /></div><p class="MsoListParagraph" style="margin:0in;mso-add-space:auto;line-height:&#xA;normal"><span style="font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">Possession
of Minimum Qualifications will be verified prior to interview and/or
appointment. If you are meeting Minimum Qualifications with education, you must
include your unofficial transcript(s)/diploma for verification. Unofficial,
original or official sealed transcripts will be required upon appointment. Applicants
with foreign transcripts/degrees must provide a transcript/degree U.S.
equivalency report evaluation that indicates the number of units and degree to
which the foreign coursework is equivalent. Here is a list of evaluation
agencies: </span><a href="https://www.naces.org/members"><span style="font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">https://www.naces.org/members</span></a><span style="font-size:12.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,sans-serif">.</span></p></span>
                </div>
            
</div>

